# Google Stitch UI Design Authority (STRICT)

All user-facing UI MUST follow `.planning/google-stitch-ui-design/` — no exceptions.

## Before writing or editing UI

1. Read `.planning/google-stitch-ui-design/DESIGN.md`
2. Read the matching screen prototype `{screen}_notion_style/code.html`
3. Read the existing React reference in `src/components/` (port, do not redesign)
4. Use `@theme` tokens from `src/index.css` / `app/globals.css` — not default shadcn/Tailwind themes

## Non-negotiable

- Monochrome document-first aesthetic; thin `#e5e5e5` borders; no card drop shadows
- Inter typography scale from DESIGN.md; Material Symbols Outlined icons
- 4px spacing grid; primary button black on white; chips/tags light gray `#f1f1f0`
- shadcn/Radix primitives OK only when restyled to Stitch tokens (D-53)

## Blocking anti-patterns

- Default shadcn theme colors, rounded-xl/2xl cards, saturated accents, glassmorphism
- Hardcoded hex drift from Stitch tokens without DESIGN.md justification
- New visual language when a Stitch screen exists — extend DESIGN.md instead

See also: `.planning/google-stitch-ui-design/SKILL.md`
